## Core Guidelines

### Command Name Should Be Clear and Descriptive

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command" OR file.path contains "commands")

**Guidance:**
📝 **Command Naming Best Practices:**

- Use clear, action-oriented names (e.g., `/refactor`, `/test`, `/document`)
- Avoid abbreviations unless universally understood
- Use kebab-case or lowercase for consistency
- Make the purpose obvious from the name alone

**Good Examples:**
- `/generate-component` - Clear purpose
- `/add-test-coverage` - Action-oriented
- `/refactor-to-repository-pattern` - Specific and descriptive

**Bad Examples:**
- `/gen` - Too vague
- `/do-stuff` - Not descriptive
- `/cmd1` - Meaningless

### Commands Should Have Single Responsibility

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command")

**Guidance:**
🎯 **Single Responsibility Principle:**

Each command should do one thing well:
- One command = One clear outcome
- Avoid commands that do multiple unrelated tasks
- Chain simple commands rather than creating complex ones

**Good:**
- `/generate-component` - Creates component only
- `/add-types` - Adds TypeScript types only
- `/create-test` - Creates test file only

**Bad:**
- `/setup-project` - Too broad, does many things
- `/fix-and-test` - Mixes concerns

### Commands Should Include Clear Documentation

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command")

**Guidance:**
📚 **Documentation Requirements:**

Every command should include:
- **Description:** What the command does (1-2 sentences)
- **Usage:** How to invoke it with examples
- **Parameters:** What inputs it accepts (if any)
- **Output:** What it produces or modifies
- **Examples:** Real-world usage scenarios

**Format:**
```
/command-name
Description: [Clear description]
Usage: /command-name [parameters]
Example: /command-name --option value
```

### Commands Should Be Reusable and Parameterizable

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command")

**Guidance:**
🔄 **Reusability Best Practices:**

- Accept parameters for flexibility (file paths, options, flags)
- Use sensible defaults when possible
- Support multiple contexts (different file types, directories)
- Avoid hard-coding specific values

**Good:**
- `/generate-component ComponentName --type=class`
- `/add-test path/to/file.ts --framework=jest`
- `/refactor --pattern=repository`

**Bad:**
- `/generate-user-component` - Too specific, not reusable
- `/fix-bug-in-app.tsx` - Hard-coded file path

### Commands Should Provide Clear Feedback

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command")

**Guidance:**
💬 **Feedback and Output:**

Commands should:
- Show progress for long-running operations
- Report success/failure clearly
- Provide actionable error messages
- Indicate what was changed/created/modified
- Offer next steps when appropriate

**Good Feedback:**
- "✅ Created component at src/components/Button.tsx"
- "⚠️ Warning: File already exists. Use --overwrite to replace."
- "❌ Error: Component name required. Usage: /generate-component <name>"

### Commands Should Handle Errors Gracefully

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command")

**Guidance:**
🛡️ **Error Handling:**

Commands should:
- Validate inputs before execution
- Check prerequisites (files exist, dependencies available)
- Provide helpful error messages with solutions
- Avoid destructive operations without confirmation
- Rollback changes when possible on failure

**Error Message Best Practices:**
- Explain what went wrong
- Suggest how to fix it
- Reference relevant documentation
- Include example of correct usage

### Commands Should Follow Consistent Patterns

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command")

**Guidance:**
🔄 **Consistency Guidelines:**

Maintain consistency across commands:
- Use same parameter format (`--flag` vs `-f`)
- Consistent naming conventions
- Similar structure and organization
- Uniform error handling approach
- Standard output format

**Example Pattern:**
```
/<action>-<target> [options]
/generate-component --name=Button --type=functional
/add-test --file=utils.ts --framework=jest
/refactor-to-pattern --pattern=repository
```

### Commands Should Be Discoverable

**Trigger Conditions:**
- Block text contains: "/" AND (block.text matches /(create|write|make|build|generate|add).*command/i OR block.text contains "slash command" OR block.text contains "custom command")

**Guidance:**
🔍 **Discoverability:**

Make commands easy to find and use:
- Use intuitive, searchable names
- Group related commands with prefixes (e.g., `/test-*`, `/generate-*`)
- Document in a central location
- Provide autocomplete hints when possible
- Include aliases for common commands

**Grouping Examples:**
- `/generate-component`, `/generate-hook`, `/generate-util`
- `/test-unit`, `/test-integration`, `/test-e2e`
- `/refactor-extract`, `/refactor-rename`, `/refactor-move`

## Code Patterns

### Required Pattern

```markdown
# ✅ Good: Clear, documented command
/generate-component
Description: Generates a new React component with TypeScript
Usage: /generate-component <name> [--type=functional|class] [--path=src/components]
Example: /generate-component Button --type=functional
Output: Creates Button.tsx with proper structure
```

### Anti-Pattern (Avoid)

```markdown
# ❌ Bad: Vague, undocumented command
/gen
[Missing: Description]
[Missing: Usage]
[Missing: Examples]
```

